# Future Awareness

## The rule
Before building any feature, read `docs/product-vision.md` and check whether the feature being built will need to connect to or support anything in a later phase.

## What this means in practice

### Before designing a data model
Check: will this table need to relate to content types added in later phases?

Example: Building the `outputs` table in V1. The roadmap says Phase 2 adds documents and Phase 5 adds tasks. All three are project-linked content. So:
- Use a consistent structure across content tables (project link, type, status, tags, metadata)
- Use a many-to-many join table for project linking (not a single `project_id` column) — because Phase 2 documents need multi-project linking
- Don't build the documents or tasks tables yet — just make sure `outputs` doesn't use a pattern that would conflict

### Before designing an API endpoint
Check: will other features need similar endpoints?

Example: Building `GET /api/outputs`. The roadmap says documents and discussions are coming. So:
- Use a consistent response shape now that works for any content type later
- Use consistent pagination, filtering, and search patterns
- Don't build `/api/documents` — just don't make `/api/outputs` a one-off pattern

### Before designing UI
Check: will this screen need to accommodate more content types?

Example: Building the project detail page for V1. The roadmap says documents, tasks, and discussions will attach to projects later. So:
- Design the project page with a tabbed or sectioned layout that can hold more sections
- Don't hardcode "Outputs" as the only content area — use a pattern that extends
- Don't build the other tabs yet

## What this rule does NOT do
- It does not build future features early
- It does not add unused columns, tables, or code "just in case"
- It does not slow down the current feature
- It does not add complexity to V1

## What it does
- It prevents painting yourself into a corner
- It leaves the right seams open for extension
- It makes Phase 2 a smooth addition, not a rewrite of Phase 1

## After building, call it out
In the change explanation (see `explain-changes.mdc`), include a section:

> **Future-proofing:** [what decisions were made with later phases in mind, and which phase they support]
